libraries: don't require X11 for a headless-only build

configure insists on X11 for every non-windows, non-macosx target here, so the
android builds stop before compiling anything:

  configure: error: Could not find X11 libraries.

No cross sysroot in this repository has X11, and bionic has none at all. The
build is already --enable-headless-only, which is exactly the case upstream
exempts: 17 carries this same elif, and 25 has it again after the X11 include
was dropped from libawt. 11 and 21 are the two releases in between that ask for
X11 regardless.

Note the comment being replaced claims libawt needs X11 headers even when
headless. If that is still true on these releases, the build will now fail on a
missing X11/*.h instead, and the headers have to be staged the way cups and
fontconfig already are -- but 25 builds headless with no X11 at all, so the
claim looks stale.

diff --git a/make/autoconf/libraries.m4 b/make/autoconf/libraries.m4
index 51d4f72..845de29 100644
--- a/make/autoconf/libraries.m4
+++ b/make/autoconf/libraries.m4
@@ -45,9 +45,11 @@ AC_DEFUN_ONCE([LIB_DETERMINE_DEPENDENCIES],
   if test "x$OPENJDK_TARGET_OS" = xwindows || test "x$OPENJDK_TARGET_OS" = xmacosx; then
     # No X11 support on windows or macosx
     NEEDS_LIB_X11=false
+  elif test "x$ENABLE_HEADLESS_ONLY" = xtrue; then
+    # No X11 support needed when building headless only
+    NEEDS_LIB_X11=false
   else
-    # All other instances need X11, even if building headless only, libawt still
-    # needs X11 headers.
+    # All other instances need X11
     NEEDS_LIB_X11=true
   fi
 
